WEBVTT

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:06.434
Captain's Log, Stardate 50074.3.

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:09.636
We have detected evidence that
a wormhole recently appeared

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:12.839
and then disappeared
in a nearby solar system.

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:15.507
We're on our way there
to investigate.

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:17.482
Based on the residual
neutrino levels,

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.075
I'd estimate it's been
at least six months

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.916
since the wormhole's
last appearance.

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:23.388
From the dispersal pattern
of the interstellar plasma,

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:25.516
it looks like it isn't fixed.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.082
It seems to be traveling
through space.

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:28.719
It may not be fixed on this end,

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:31.595
but if it's shown up in the
same location more than once,

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.997
it's possible its exit point
is constant

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.898
and it's wagging
around the Delta Quadrant

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.163
like the tail on a dog.

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.500
Approaching

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:40.472
the last-known coordinates
of the wormhole, Captain.

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:41.599
All stop.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.939
Mr. Kim, initiate
continuous neutrino scans.

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:45.171
Aye, Captain.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.873
Mr. Tuvok, scan the planets
in this system for life signs.

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:49.313
Maybe there's
someone around here

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:51.112
who can give us
some helpful information.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.982
I am picking up
an M-Class atmosphere

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:54.213
on the second planet.

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:56.017
Humanoid life signs.

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:57.387
However, metallurgic

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:59.949
analysis indicates
a preindustrial civilization,

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:02.291
a Bronze-Age level
of technology.

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:04.353
Curious, Captain.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:05.921
What is?

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.660
I'm detecting evidence
that these people

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.225
have had contact
with the Alpha Quadrant.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.135
What kind of evidence?

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:13.605
It is a modulated
energy discharge

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:17.076
that appears to be consistent
with the recent use...

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.805
of a replicator.

00:03:15.159 --> 00:03:16.490
If they've got a replicator,

00:03:16.527 --> 00:03:20.122
it could mean the wormhole
leads to the Alpha Quadrant

00:03:20.164 --> 00:03:21.461
and that someone's
traveled through it.

00:03:21.499 --> 00:03:23.694
I appreciate
your enthusiasm, Ensign,

00:03:23.735 --> 00:03:25.396
but before we indulge
in too much speculation,

00:03:25.436 --> 00:03:28.303
let's see if we can back up your
assumptions with some facts.

00:03:28.339 --> 00:03:30.569
Commander Chakotay,
I want you and Lieutenant Paris

00:03:30.608 --> 00:03:32.599
to go down to that planet
and have a look around.

00:03:32.644 --> 00:03:35.078
Launch a high-resolution
reconnaissance probe

00:03:35.113 --> 00:03:36.171
to gather information

00:03:36.214 --> 00:03:38.239
about the local population's
dress and appearance.

00:03:38.283 --> 00:03:39.443
Aye, Captain.

00:03:39.484 --> 00:03:40.974
In the meantime, Ensign,
why don't you

00:03:41.052 --> 00:03:43.077
and Lieutenant Torres
get started on a phase profile

00:03:43.121 --> 00:03:46.090
of this elusive wormhole's
neutrino emissions.

00:03:46.124 --> 00:03:49.719
Let's see if we can confirm
that it leads

00:03:49.761 --> 00:03:51.956
to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:03:51.996 --> 00:03:56.558
Captain's Log, Stardate 50074.5.

00:03:56.601 --> 00:03:59.195
Based on information provided
by the probe,

00:03:59.237 --> 00:04:01.364
we have replicated local attire

00:04:01.406 --> 00:04:03.670
for Commander Chakotay
and Lieutenant Paris.

00:04:03.708 --> 00:04:06.268
They have gone to the surface
to investigate.

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.965
This is where we picked up
a replicator signature?

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:30.830
Hard to believe, isn't it?

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:34.730
"Oh, those many years ago,

00:04:34.772 --> 00:04:38.333
"the people's hearts
were sad and low,

00:04:38.376 --> 00:04:41.539
"then the Sages
to the city came.

00:04:41.579 --> 00:04:45.345
"They came upon a burning flame.

00:04:45.383 --> 00:04:48.216
"Just as the seer
said they would,

00:04:48.252 --> 00:04:52.552
they lifted
Takar's blinding hood."

00:04:54.592 --> 00:04:55.889
Well...

00:04:58.763 --> 00:05:00.788
what did you think?

00:05:00.832 --> 00:05:02.857
It was...

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:03.924
uh, very nice.

00:05:03.968 --> 00:05:05.595
Nice?

00:05:05.636 --> 00:05:08.332
I'll wager you've never heard
"The Song of the Sages"

00:05:08.373 --> 00:05:13.072
more beautifully
or faithfully recited.

00:05:14.112 --> 00:05:16.103
He's got a point.

00:05:16.147 --> 00:05:18.911
We have never heard
"The Song of the Sages"

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:20.850
more beautifully recited.

00:05:20.885 --> 00:05:23.945
As you know,
the first verse is free,

00:05:24.022 --> 00:05:26.684
but the next verse will
cost you three frangs.

00:05:26.724 --> 00:05:28.248
I'm sorry. Not today.

00:05:28.292 --> 00:05:30.226
But I need money...

00:05:30.261 --> 00:05:32.388
for ointment for my eye.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:33.761
Please, gentlemen...

00:05:33.798 --> 00:05:35.356
Oh, go away, old man.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.367
Can't you see?

00:05:36.401 --> 00:05:37.663
These are men of commerce.

00:05:37.702 --> 00:05:41.365
They have no business
with your silly poems.

00:05:41.406 --> 00:05:45.672
And may I say, gentlemen,
you both have very fine shoes.

00:05:46.677 --> 00:05:47.701
Excuse me?

00:05:47.745 --> 00:05:49.975
Well, the Sages say
you can tell a great deal

00:05:50.048 --> 00:05:51.413
about a man from his shoes,

00:05:51.449 --> 00:05:55.283
and I can tell from your shoes
that you're men of refinement...

00:05:55.319 --> 00:05:57.310
affluence.

00:05:57.355 --> 00:05:59.255
We've really got to be going.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:00.951
Well, you're obviously
new in Takar.

00:06:00.992 --> 00:06:03.654
Perhaps I could
interest you in some property.

00:06:03.694 --> 00:06:04.718
No, thank you.

00:06:04.762 --> 00:06:06.627
We're not planning
on settling here.

00:06:06.664 --> 00:06:07.926
What about some transportation?

00:06:07.999 --> 00:06:09.899
The Sages say "time's an asset."

00:06:09.934 --> 00:06:13.131
And you shouldn't
waste your assets

00:06:13.171 --> 00:06:14.729
walking everywhere you go.

00:06:14.772 --> 00:06:17.935
You'd be wearing out
those fine shoes of yours.

00:06:18.976 --> 00:06:21.877
I'm sorry,
but we're really not interested.

00:06:21.913 --> 00:06:22.880
Tom?

00:06:22.914 --> 00:06:24.848
Excuse me.

00:06:27.351 --> 00:06:30.946
I'm picking up a narrow-band
EM dampening field

00:06:30.988 --> 00:06:32.148
around that building.

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:33.487
It looks like
some sort of temple.

00:06:33.524 --> 00:06:35.355
Then I'd say the temple's
where we ought to look.

00:06:35.393 --> 00:06:38.055
Oh, thank the Sages I found you.

00:06:38.096 --> 00:06:40.963
You can't enter the temple
without wearing your ears.

00:06:41.065 --> 00:06:42.692
Look, friend,
I thought I told you...

00:06:42.733 --> 00:06:45.224
What do you mean
"wearing your ears?"

00:06:46.804 --> 00:06:49.272
You're really not Takarian,
are you?

00:06:49.307 --> 00:06:50.740
Nobody visits the temple

00:06:50.775 --> 00:06:53.573
without displaying
at least one ear.

00:07:00.351 --> 00:07:01.909
It must be some sort of fetish.

00:07:01.953 --> 00:07:04.319
If you're not wearing an ear,
you could be fined,

00:07:04.355 --> 00:07:05.822
even arrested.

00:07:05.857 --> 00:07:07.688
Wouldn't want that to happen.

00:07:07.725 --> 00:07:09.215
And let me guess.

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:10.284
It just so happens

00:07:10.328 --> 00:07:12.728
that you could sell us
a couple of these ears.

00:07:12.763 --> 00:07:14.754
As a matter of fact...

00:07:14.799 --> 00:07:16.323
I can.

00:07:30.648 --> 00:07:32.639
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:07:32.683 --> 00:07:34.583
I've been asked
to join Lieutenant Torres

00:07:34.619 --> 00:07:36.484
and Ensign Kim
in the Science Lab

00:07:36.521 --> 00:07:39.718
to hear what they've termed
as "very exciting news."

00:07:39.757 --> 00:07:40.849
We've been able to confirm

00:07:40.892 --> 00:07:43.053
that the wormhole does lead
to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:07:43.094 --> 00:07:45.460
The problem is that on this end,

00:07:45.496 --> 00:07:47.464
it's jumping from point
to point so quickly

00:07:47.498 --> 00:07:48.931
that even at maximum warp,

00:07:48.966 --> 00:07:51.059
by the time we got to
its next probable location,

00:07:51.102 --> 00:07:52.296
it would be gone.

00:07:52.336 --> 00:07:53.633
So we were thinking

00:07:53.671 --> 00:07:55.730
if you can't bring
the ship to the wormhole,

00:07:55.773 --> 00:07:58.071
bring the wormhole to the ship.

00:07:58.109 --> 00:08:00.270
We've detected
a subspace instability

00:08:00.311 --> 00:08:01.710
at our current location

00:08:01.746 --> 00:08:03.839
that's a result of the
wormhole's last appearance here.

00:08:03.881 --> 00:08:06.907
If we could somehow amplify
and polarize that instability,

00:08:07.018 --> 00:08:09.748
we might be able to get
the wormhole to reappear.

00:08:09.787 --> 00:08:13.484
Sort of like using a magnet
to move a compass needle.

00:08:13.524 --> 00:08:14.513
The question is:

00:08:14.559 --> 00:08:17.187
How do we polarize
the instability?

00:08:17.228 --> 00:08:20.095
Uh, we haven't figured
that part out yet.

00:08:23.668 --> 00:08:27.570
Gentlemen, as the Sages say,
your goods are now my goods.

00:08:27.605 --> 00:08:29.573
And my feet are now cold.

00:08:29.607 --> 00:08:30.733
Perhaps I could

00:08:30.775 --> 00:08:34.142
interest you in some
discounted mining futures.

00:08:34.178 --> 00:08:35.509
Don't push your luck.

00:08:35.546 --> 00:08:37.036
You know, so far,

00:08:37.081 --> 00:08:39.242
I can't say that I like
this town very much.

00:08:55.967 --> 00:08:57.935
On the other hand...

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:08.041
My friends...

00:09:08.079 --> 00:09:09.808
the Holy Sages.

00:09:26.864 --> 00:09:29.856
Behold the Holy Icon.

00:09:38.075 --> 00:09:40.236
Greed is eternal.

00:09:40.278 --> 00:09:42.610
Greed
is eternal.

00:09:42.647 --> 00:09:45.411
Greed is eternal.

00:09:45.449 --> 00:09:48.543
Greed
is eternal.

00:09:50.788 --> 00:09:54.280
Now what other wisdom
have you learned from the Sages?

00:09:54.325 --> 00:09:57.226
"A wise man can hear profit
in the wind."

00:09:57.261 --> 00:10:01.095
A wise man
can hear profit in the wind.

00:10:01.132 --> 00:10:02.292
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:10:02.333 --> 00:10:03.630
Janeway here.

00:10:03.668 --> 00:10:05.329
We found the replicator,
Captain.

00:10:07.338 --> 00:10:10.136
A wise man can hear profit
in the wind.

00:10:14.278 --> 00:10:17.145
And now, dear friends,
in our great beneficence,

00:10:17.181 --> 00:10:19.376
we will allow you
to come forward

00:10:19.417 --> 00:10:23.547
to honor our greatness
and glorify our generosity.

00:10:23.587 --> 00:10:26.681
Approach the Holy Sages.

00:10:29.894 --> 00:10:33.091
Approach your gods
and speak your heart.

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:37.725
Ehh!

00:10:42.606 --> 00:10:44.130
I am a sandal maker

00:10:44.175 --> 00:10:45.608
from the poorest
quarter of the city.

00:10:45.643 --> 00:10:47.133
The laziest, you mean.

00:10:47.178 --> 00:10:49.373
Speak, my friend.

00:10:49.413 --> 00:10:51.381
What is your business
with the Sages?

00:10:51.415 --> 00:10:53.212
I am in need of assistance.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.150
My sandal shop is failing.

00:10:55.186 --> 00:10:57.017
I can no longer feed my family.

00:10:57.088 --> 00:10:58.680
Same old song.

00:10:58.723 --> 00:11:03.683
My wife and her mother,
my five children, the baby.

00:11:03.728 --> 00:11:07.255
That's seven employees...
eight, if you count the infant.

00:11:07.298 --> 00:11:09.425
How can your shop be failing?

00:11:09.467 --> 00:11:11.867
You're not paying them, are you?

00:11:11.902 --> 00:11:13.733
My mother-in-law is ill.

00:11:13.771 --> 00:11:15.932
My children are very young.

00:11:15.973 --> 00:11:19.238
Oh. Don't tell me
none of them are working.

00:11:19.276 --> 00:11:22.973
Ignorant, lobeless fools!

00:11:23.013 --> 00:11:27.313
Exploitation begins at home.

00:11:27.351 --> 00:11:30.479
Exploitation
begins at home.

00:11:31.789 --> 00:11:36.089
Exploitation
begins at home.

00:11:36.127 --> 00:11:38.857
Exploitation begins at home.

00:11:45.269 --> 00:11:47.100
I understand my mistake

00:11:47.138 --> 00:11:48.935
and I promise
to begin exploiting my family

00:11:48.973 --> 00:11:50.531
before the end of the day,

00:11:50.574 --> 00:11:55.011
but could I have some food
and some medicine?

00:11:55.112 --> 00:11:56.409
Ohh!

00:11:56.447 --> 00:11:58.415
Until my business improves.

00:11:58.449 --> 00:12:01.850
You shall have something
far more valuable...

00:12:01.886 --> 00:12:04.946
one copy of The Rules
of Acquisition.

00:12:05.022 --> 00:12:06.922
Cheapest binding possible.

00:12:20.738 --> 00:12:22.729
That'll be ten frangs.

00:12:22.773 --> 00:12:24.263
But I...

00:12:32.283 --> 00:12:33.511
That's all for today.

00:12:33.551 --> 00:12:35.212
You may return tomorrow.

00:12:38.289 --> 00:12:40.757
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:12:40.791 --> 00:12:42.190
The away team has returned

00:12:42.226 --> 00:12:43.989
with some very disturbing
observations

00:12:44.094 --> 00:12:46.585
about the situation
on the planet.

00:12:46.630 --> 00:12:48.120
It seems the people
have a myth...

00:12:48.165 --> 00:12:51.259
an epic poem called
"The Song of the Sages,"

00:12:51.302 --> 00:12:52.792
which predicts the arrival

00:12:52.837 --> 00:12:55.271
of two demigods
from the sky, the Sages,

00:12:55.306 --> 00:12:58.241
who would rule over the people
as benevolent protectors.

00:12:58.275 --> 00:13:00.743
But these Ferengi are anything
but benevolent.

00:13:00.778 --> 00:13:02.837
What they've done is co-opt
the local mythology

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:05.906
by using advanced technology
like the replicator

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:06.939
to convince the people

00:13:07.051 --> 00:13:08.916
that they're the two Sages
spoken of in the poem.

00:13:08.953 --> 00:13:10.443
Of course, being Ferengi,

00:13:10.488 --> 00:13:12.353
they haven't just
co-opted the mythology.

00:13:12.389 --> 00:13:15.381
They've cornered the market...
on everything.

00:13:15.426 --> 00:13:16.916
It's disgusting, Captain.

00:13:16.961 --> 00:13:19.122
The two Ferengi live
in a palatial temple,

00:13:19.163 --> 00:13:21.631
while the people are lucky to
have a roof over their heads.

00:13:21.665 --> 00:13:23.895
Apparently, it wasn't
always like that.

00:13:23.934 --> 00:13:25.629
According to the people
that we met,

00:13:25.669 --> 00:13:28.832
before the Ferengi came, the
society may have been primitive,

00:13:28.873 --> 00:13:29.965
but it was flourishing.

00:13:30.074 --> 00:13:31.735
What I'd like to know

00:13:31.775 --> 00:13:34.471
is how two Ferengi
got to the Delta Quadrant.

00:13:34.512 --> 00:13:36.537
We've been looking
into that. Mr. Tuvok.

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:38.946
According to Starfleet
computer records,

00:13:38.983 --> 00:13:40.348
approximately seven years ago,

00:13:40.384 --> 00:13:43.512
the Federation Starship
Enterprise hosted negotiations

00:13:43.554 --> 00:13:45.818
for ownership
of the Barzan wormhole.

00:13:45.856 --> 00:13:48.347
Included among the bidding
parties were two Ferengi...

00:13:48.392 --> 00:13:51.452
minor functionaries
known as Arridor and Kol.

00:13:51.495 --> 00:13:53.486
And this Barzan wormhole...

00:13:53.531 --> 00:13:55.965
it's the same one
we've discovered now?

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:59.367
Apparently, but we've confirmed
what nobody knew at the time.

00:13:59.403 --> 00:14:02.304
The wormhole is fixed
in the Alpha Quadrant,

00:14:02.339 --> 00:14:04.273
but in the Delta Quadrant,
it jumps around.

00:14:04.308 --> 00:14:06.142
It turned out to be worthless.

00:14:06.275 --> 00:14:08.072
But the Ferengi
were not aware of that,

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:09.407
and during a nefarious attempt

00:14:09.445 --> 00:14:11.436
to secure
the wormhole for themselves,

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:14.677
they were pulled into it and
deposited in the Delta Quadrant.

00:14:14.717 --> 00:14:17.413
Now that we've found them, what
are we going to do with them?

00:14:17.453 --> 00:14:19.216
Well, I certainly don't intend
to leave them here

00:14:19.255 --> 00:14:21.655
to continue exploiting
an innocent society.

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:23.089
How are you two
coming with getting

00:14:23.125 --> 00:14:25.184
the wormhole back here
and reopened?

00:14:25.227 --> 00:14:27.957
We've been bombarding the area
of the subspace instability

00:14:27.997 --> 00:14:29.225
with verteron particles.

00:14:29.265 --> 00:14:31.665
So far, everything is going
according to plan,

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:32.962
but it's tricky.

00:14:33.035 --> 00:14:34.696
There are a hundred factors

00:14:34.737 --> 00:14:36.329
that could deflect
it from this sector...

00:14:36.372 --> 00:14:38.499
a gravimetric shift,
a solar flare...

00:14:38.541 --> 00:14:40.168
And even if we're lucky
enough to get it here,

00:14:40.209 --> 00:14:41.369
it won't be around for long.

00:14:41.410 --> 00:14:42.900
We'll have a very short
window of opportunity

00:14:42.945 --> 00:14:43.969
to get through.

00:14:44.046 --> 00:14:46.207
Well, if we can get
the wormhole here,

00:14:46.248 --> 00:14:49.183
we'll be taking two additional
passengers with us.

00:14:49.218 --> 00:14:51.743
We'll turn them over to Ferengi
authorities when we get there.

00:14:51.787 --> 00:14:53.516
Captain, I must remind you

00:14:53.556 --> 00:14:55.956
that the Ferengi are not
members of the Federation.

00:14:55.991 --> 00:14:58.551
They are not bound
by the Prime Directive,

00:14:58.594 --> 00:15:00.425
nor would it seem
that the Prime Directive

00:15:00.462 --> 00:15:01.656
would allow us to interfere

00:15:01.697 --> 00:15:03.927
with the internal affairs
of this society,

00:15:03.966 --> 00:15:06.958
as much as we may disapprove
of what the Ferengi are doing.

00:15:09.471 --> 00:15:12.133
The Federation did host
the negotiations,

00:15:12.174 --> 00:15:14.802
and if it weren't
for those negotiations,

00:15:14.843 --> 00:15:17.573
the Ferengi wouldn't be here.

00:15:17.613 --> 00:15:19.911
So one could say...

00:15:19.949 --> 00:15:22.543
without being unreasonable,
I think,

00:15:22.585 --> 00:15:26.612
that the Federation is partially
responsible for what's happened

00:15:26.655 --> 00:15:30.887
and therefore, duty bound
to correct the situation.

00:15:33.295 --> 00:15:37.391
That is a most logical
interpretation, Captain.

00:15:37.433 --> 00:15:40.266
143...

00:15:40.302 --> 00:15:42.270
144...

00:15:42.304 --> 00:15:44.738
145...

00:15:44.773 --> 00:15:47.139
146...

00:15:47.176 --> 00:15:50.737
147, 148...

00:15:54.984 --> 00:15:58.283
Profits from the Ga'nah Province
are down.

00:15:58.320 --> 00:15:59.787
Hmm?

00:15:59.822 --> 00:16:01.915
Are you listening to me?

00:16:01.991 --> 00:16:05.825
I said profits from the Ga'nah
Province are down.

00:16:05.861 --> 00:16:07.123
Down?!

00:16:07.162 --> 00:16:08.925
Profits are down?

00:16:08.998 --> 00:16:11.091
Hey, both of you leave me alone.

00:16:11.133 --> 00:16:15.092
Can't you see I'm trying
to conduct business here?

00:16:15.137 --> 00:16:16.866
I'm... sorry...

00:16:17.873 --> 00:16:18.840
Arridor.

00:16:18.874 --> 00:16:19.841
It's just that...

00:16:19.875 --> 00:16:22.343
they can't get enough
of my lobes.

00:16:22.378 --> 00:16:23.868
Where were we?

00:16:23.912 --> 00:16:26.346
Oh, yeah.
Profits are down?

00:16:26.382 --> 00:16:29.476
And what are we going to do
about it?

00:16:29.518 --> 00:16:31.145
What are you looking at me for?

00:16:31.186 --> 00:16:32.710
Ask that idiot Kafar.

00:16:32.755 --> 00:16:35.952
He's in charge of collections
in the Ga'nah Province.

00:16:36.058 --> 00:16:37.650
Kafar!

00:16:39.194 --> 00:16:41.094
You called, Great Sage?

00:16:41.130 --> 00:16:44.065
What is the 95th Rule
of Acquisition?

00:16:44.099 --> 00:16:45.566
Huh!

00:16:45.601 --> 00:16:47.159
"Expand or die"?

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:50.604
He knows the rules
better than you do.

00:16:50.639 --> 00:16:51.901
He does not.

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:53.237
And where is it

00:16:53.275 --> 00:16:56.244
we've been trying
to expand... this month?

00:16:56.278 --> 00:16:58.678
Into the Ga'nah Province,
Great Sage.

00:16:58.714 --> 00:17:01.706
And who is in charge
of collections

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:03.240
in the Ga'nah Province?

00:17:03.285 --> 00:17:04.843
I am, Great Sage.

00:17:04.887 --> 00:17:07.185
Then why are profits down,
you idiot?!

00:17:07.222 --> 00:17:08.814
Where's our money?!

00:17:08.857 --> 00:17:10.518
Please forgive me, Lesser Sage.

00:17:10.559 --> 00:17:13.926
Oh, I told you to stop
calling me...

00:17:42.424 --> 00:17:43.948
Who are you?

00:17:43.992 --> 00:17:47.951
Captain Kathryn Janeway of the
Federation Starship Voyager.

00:17:48.063 --> 00:17:49.655
The Federation?

00:17:49.698 --> 00:17:51.689
Shut up, Kol.
Let me handle this.

00:17:56.572 --> 00:17:58.540
What, may I ask

00:17:58.574 --> 00:18:01.475
is the Federation doing
in the Delta Quadrant?

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:03.603
It's a long story,
but suffice it to say,

00:18:03.645 --> 00:18:06.205
we've been stranded here
for the past two years.

00:18:06.248 --> 00:18:09.081
We're on our way back
to the Alpha Quadrant

00:18:09.118 --> 00:18:11.086
and we're taking you with us.

00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:12.417
This is an outrage.

00:18:12.454 --> 00:18:14.684
We won't allow you to tr...

00:18:14.723 --> 00:18:16.588
You're crazy.

00:18:16.625 --> 00:18:18.855
It would take decades
to get back from here.

00:18:18.894 --> 00:18:21.089
Show them, Mr. Tuvok.

00:18:23.098 --> 00:18:24.395
We have been bombarding

00:18:24.433 --> 00:18:27.163
a local subspace instability
with verteron particles.

00:18:27.202 --> 00:18:30.501
If all goes according to plan,
the Barzan wormhole

00:18:30.539 --> 00:18:32.632
should reopen
at our present location

00:18:32.674 --> 00:18:33.766
in a matter of hours.

00:18:33.809 --> 00:18:36.243
And if all doesn't go
according to plan?

00:18:36.278 --> 00:18:39.770
One way or another,
you're coming with us.

00:18:39.815 --> 00:18:41.783
We've been kidnapped...

00:18:41.817 --> 00:18:43.614
snatched...

00:18:43.652 --> 00:18:46.621
from the embrace of bliss.

00:18:46.655 --> 00:18:48.418
It's all over.

00:18:48.457 --> 00:18:51.483
No more limitless profits...

00:18:51.527 --> 00:18:55.964
no more unquestioning adulation
of the masses...

00:18:56.031 --> 00:19:00.195
no more quadruple lobe rubs.

00:19:00.235 --> 00:19:03.864
If I'm not mistaken, Captain,
the Federation has rules,

00:19:03.906 --> 00:19:05.533
and those rules forbid you

00:19:05.574 --> 00:19:07.872
to interfere
with indigenous cultures.

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:09.605
What about your interference?

00:19:09.645 --> 00:19:11.169
You've taken
these people's religion

00:19:11.213 --> 00:19:13.909
and manipulated it
for your own selfish purposes,

00:19:13.982 --> 00:19:16.416
pretended to be their Sages.

00:19:16.452 --> 00:19:19.285
Who's to say we aren't
their Sages, Captain?

00:19:19.321 --> 00:19:20.845
Don't be ridiculous.

00:19:20.889 --> 00:19:24.825
The song is sung of Sages
who can perform miracles,

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:28.261
which, thanks to our replicator,
we do.

00:19:28.297 --> 00:19:30.322
The song is sung of men

00:19:30.365 --> 00:19:33.528
coming from the sky
on a burning flame...

00:19:33.569 --> 00:19:35.594
when we crash-landed our shuttle

00:19:35.637 --> 00:19:37.730
in their quaint
little town square,

00:19:37.773 --> 00:19:44.406
trailing behind us a roaring
ribbon of burning plasma.

00:19:44.446 --> 00:19:47.176
You mean we really
are the Sages?

00:19:50.786 --> 00:19:53.721
The point is, Captain,
that these people

00:19:53.755 --> 00:19:57.953
have believed for centuries
that gods, known as the Sages,

00:19:58.026 --> 00:20:00.221
would deliver them
from their strife.

00:20:00.262 --> 00:20:02.253
To them...

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:07.401
we are those Sages.

00:20:07.436 --> 00:20:10.462
What happens to a people
when they lose their gods?

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:13.234
Despair...

00:20:13.275 --> 00:20:14.242
Mm-hmm.

00:20:14.276 --> 00:20:15.243
Fear...

00:20:15.277 --> 00:20:16.244
Mmm...

00:20:16.278 --> 00:20:18.473
confusion.

00:20:18.514 --> 00:20:20.141
And how can you...

00:20:21.149 --> 00:20:23.276
as a moral people,

00:20:23.318 --> 00:20:26.583
blithely tear down
the spiritual structure

00:20:26.622 --> 00:20:28.419
that has supported a community

00:20:28.457 --> 00:20:31.858
since before their gods
were flesh?

00:20:31.894 --> 00:20:34.829
What would you
be leaving them with?

00:20:34.863 --> 00:20:37.161
Tell us, Arridor, tell us.

00:20:37.199 --> 00:20:38.427
Darkness...

00:20:39.535 --> 00:20:41.366
doubt...

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:44.334
hopelessness.

00:20:44.373 --> 00:20:47.342
That was beautiful.

00:20:52.014 --> 00:20:53.743
Mr. Tuvok...

00:20:55.817 --> 00:20:57.910
transport them back
to the surface.

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:06.518
We did it, Arridor.

00:21:06.562 --> 00:21:07.824
We won.

00:21:25.814 --> 00:21:27.543
We can't just leave
the Ferengi there

00:21:27.583 --> 00:21:29.551
to continue exploiting
those poor people.

00:21:29.585 --> 00:21:30.643
But Arridor is right.

00:21:30.686 --> 00:21:32.483
We can't kidnap
their gods either.

00:21:32.521 --> 00:21:34.455
What other option is there?

00:21:34.489 --> 00:21:37.424
What if the gods
didn't just disappear

00:21:37.459 --> 00:21:39.188
suddenly and inexplicably?

00:21:39.227 --> 00:21:42.685
What if they left
voluntarily? Gracefully?

00:21:42.731 --> 00:21:43.891
The gods would be gone,

00:21:43.932 --> 00:21:45.923
but the people would
be prepared for it,

00:21:45.968 --> 00:21:46.935
and they might accept it

00:21:46.969 --> 00:21:48.231
as a natural,
ordained occurrence.

00:21:48.270 --> 00:21:49.328
Exactly.

00:21:49.371 --> 00:21:52.306
But how do we get two Ferengi
to just walk away

00:21:52.341 --> 00:21:54.673
from a monopoly
on an entire economy?

00:21:54.710 --> 00:21:56.575
What motivates a Ferengi?

00:21:56.612 --> 00:21:57.806
Profit.

00:21:57.846 --> 00:21:58.813
Then we must find a way

00:21:58.847 --> 00:22:01.111
to make it more profitable
for them to leave.

00:22:01.149 --> 00:22:03.310
Or less profitable to stay.

00:22:03.352 --> 00:22:05.582
How do we do that?

00:22:05.621 --> 00:22:08.055
We have to out-Ferengi...

00:22:08.090 --> 00:22:10.490
the Ferengi.

00:22:13.595 --> 00:22:15.460
Mmm.

00:22:15.497 --> 00:22:16.623
There we are.

00:22:16.665 --> 00:22:20.101
I've reconfigured
the matter/antimatter generator

00:22:20.135 --> 00:22:22.296
to produce
an ionic disruption field

00:22:22.337 --> 00:22:23.736
around the temple square.

00:22:23.772 --> 00:22:25.865
No more unexpected beam-outs.

00:22:25.907 --> 00:22:29.399
Let's see how smart those
hu-mans think they are now.

00:22:31.613 --> 00:22:32.671
Kafar!

00:22:34.249 --> 00:22:35.716
You called, Great Sage?

00:22:35.751 --> 00:22:37.981
Find out who has the audacity

00:22:38.020 --> 00:22:39.988
to disturb us in
our Divine Vault.

00:22:40.088 --> 00:22:41.282
Uh...

00:22:41.323 --> 00:22:42.881
And make it quick.

00:22:46.128 --> 00:22:48.392
Who has the audacity
to disturb the Holy Sages

00:22:48.430 --> 00:22:50.625
in their Divine Vault?

00:22:54.770 --> 00:22:56.533
- Grand Nagus!
- Grand Nagus!

00:22:59.174 --> 00:23:01.699
Not the Grand Nagus.

00:23:01.743 --> 00:23:03.938
I'm his official messenger...

00:23:04.012 --> 00:23:05.877
the Grand Proxy.

00:23:10.852 --> 00:23:14.344
But, Grand Proxy,
how did you?

00:23:14.389 --> 00:23:15.947
Through the Barzan wormhole.

00:23:15.991 --> 00:23:18.152
The hu-mans stabilized it

00:23:18.193 --> 00:23:19.888
temporarily,
and were kind enough

00:23:19.928 --> 00:23:21.623
to send a probe through

00:23:21.663 --> 00:23:26.930
informing us of your...
impressive operation.

00:23:29.404 --> 00:23:33.602
Well, of course the Grand Nagus,
or his official messenger

00:23:33.642 --> 00:23:37.510
the Grand Proxy, is always
welcome in our little world...

00:23:37.546 --> 00:23:40.845
our rather poverty-stricken
little world...

00:23:40.882 --> 00:23:43.214
and we're thrilled
he has taken an interest

00:23:43.251 --> 00:23:45.776
in our very modest operation.

00:23:45.821 --> 00:23:47.846
If I were you,

00:23:47.889 --> 00:23:51.325
I'd save the groveling
for the Nagus himself.

00:23:51.359 --> 00:23:54.988
Y-You mean, the Grand Nagus
is coming here, too?

00:23:55.097 --> 00:23:58.828
Of course not, you idiot.

00:23:58.867 --> 00:24:00.562
You two are going to him.

00:24:00.602 --> 00:24:03.537
You've been recalled.

00:24:03.572 --> 00:24:04.539
Recalled?

00:24:04.573 --> 00:24:05.540
We're ruined.

00:24:05.574 --> 00:24:07.269
You will be leaving immediately.

00:24:07.309 --> 00:24:10.107
This is not a time
to lose one's lobes.

00:24:10.145 --> 00:24:11.737
I'll think of something.

00:24:18.987 --> 00:24:22.115
Perhaps the Grand Nagus
doesn't understand

00:24:22.157 --> 00:24:25.854
that profits in this market
depend upon our presence.

00:24:25.894 --> 00:24:31.264
You see, to these people,
we're, well... gods, actually.

00:24:31.299 --> 00:24:34.632
Without us to make the
fools cower in submission,

00:24:34.669 --> 00:24:36.694
there will be
no profits to be had.

00:24:36.738 --> 00:24:40.196
The Grand Nagus knows
all about your little scheme...

00:24:40.242 --> 00:24:42.767
"The Song of the Sages"
and all the rest of it.

00:24:42.811 --> 00:24:43.800
Very clever.

00:24:43.845 --> 00:24:46.143
But he wants you
and all your acquisitions

00:24:46.181 --> 00:24:49.378
back on Ferenginar before
the wormhole closes again.

00:24:49.417 --> 00:24:52.716
I'm sure the Grand Nagus
wouldn't want to lose

00:24:52.754 --> 00:24:55.985
such a lucrative revenue stream.

00:24:56.057 --> 00:24:59.356
The wormhole seems to open
and close on its own

00:24:59.394 --> 00:25:00.827
every seven or eight years.

00:25:00.862 --> 00:25:03.797
We would be willing
to forward a fair share

00:25:03.832 --> 00:25:06.300
of the profits
every time it does.

00:25:06.334 --> 00:25:08.529
Say, hmm... 20 percent?

00:25:10.205 --> 00:25:12.036
That's coming out of your half.

00:25:12.073 --> 00:25:13.267
Shut up.

00:25:13.308 --> 00:25:15.367
The Grand Nagus has no intention

00:25:15.410 --> 00:25:18.436
of losing profits
from this market.

00:25:18.480 --> 00:25:20.675
That's why he's already
got a team of scientists

00:25:20.715 --> 00:25:23.206
investigating
the hu-man's technology...

00:25:23.251 --> 00:25:26.448
to see if we can find a way
to open and close the wormhole

00:25:26.488 --> 00:25:28.454
whenever we want.

00:25:28.587 --> 00:25:31.852
Then perhaps the Grand Nagus
could simply recall one of us

00:25:31.890 --> 00:25:34.950
and leave the other behind
to administer the operation.

00:25:34.993 --> 00:25:37.427
You could take Kol
back with you.

00:25:37.463 --> 00:25:39.192
Hey, wait a minute!
I don't think that...

00:25:39.231 --> 00:25:40.698
That's enough!

00:25:40.732 --> 00:25:42.962
The Grand Nagus
has recalled you both.

00:25:43.068 --> 00:25:45.127
It's nonnegotiable.

00:25:45.170 --> 00:25:47.730
Of course, the Nagus

00:25:47.773 --> 00:25:50.435
doesn't want to upset
the local population.

00:25:50.476 --> 00:25:53.070
He may want to send others
in your place.

00:25:53.111 --> 00:25:56.376
That's why he wants you
to make a little speech

00:25:56.415 --> 00:25:58.508
telling the people that their
Holy Sages have been recalled

00:25:58.550 --> 00:25:59.710
to the Divine Treasury,

00:25:59.751 --> 00:26:02.219
or whatever it is the people
around here call it.

00:26:02.254 --> 00:26:04.620
Then he wants you
to tell them not to worry...

00:26:04.656 --> 00:26:06.715
that everything
will be all right without you.

00:26:06.758 --> 00:26:10.922
Then he wants you to thank them
for their generosity.

00:26:10.963 --> 00:26:12.453
Thank them?

00:26:12.498 --> 00:26:15.899
The 299th Rule of Acquisition...

00:26:15.934 --> 00:26:19.461
"Whenever you exploit someone,
it never hurts to thank them.

00:26:19.505 --> 00:26:23.407
That way, it's easier
to exploit them the next time."

00:26:23.442 --> 00:26:24.534
Wait a minute.

00:26:24.576 --> 00:26:28.945
There's only 285
Rules of Acquisition.

00:26:29.014 --> 00:26:31.710
You've been gone
a very long time.

00:26:35.087 --> 00:26:36.452
Oh...

00:26:36.488 --> 00:26:40.720
By the way, did I mention
that the Nagus is appropriating

00:26:40.759 --> 00:26:41.953
all your holdings?

00:26:42.027 --> 00:26:43.619
- What?
- All?

00:26:43.662 --> 00:26:45.220
All.

00:26:45.264 --> 00:26:49.291
The least you can do is
let us keep the females.

00:26:49.334 --> 00:26:53.930
I'll be back in 20 minutes
to approve your speech.

00:26:53.972 --> 00:26:55.769
I suggest you start writing.

00:26:59.244 --> 00:27:00.302
You!

00:27:00.345 --> 00:27:01.437
Come with me!

00:27:01.480 --> 00:27:04.210
Of course, Greater Sage.

00:27:08.387 --> 00:27:11.185
What are we going to do?

00:27:11.223 --> 00:27:15.785
What a Ferengi always does
in a situation this grave.

00:27:15.827 --> 00:27:16.794
Panic?

00:27:16.828 --> 00:27:18.796
No, you idiot!

00:27:18.830 --> 00:27:22.288
He goes to the Rules
of Acquisition.

00:27:22.334 --> 00:27:23.494
Oh.

00:27:23.535 --> 00:27:27.301
Unabridged and fully annotated
with all 47 commentaries,

00:27:27.339 --> 00:27:29.671
all 900 major
and minor judgments,

00:27:29.708 --> 00:27:32.700
all 10,000
considered opinions.

00:27:32.744 --> 00:27:37.408
There is a Rule
for every conceivable situation.

00:27:39.251 --> 00:27:42.414
Looks like Neelix is pulling off
quite a performance.

00:27:44.423 --> 00:27:45.447
There you are.

00:27:45.490 --> 00:27:46.479
Don't push.

00:27:46.525 --> 00:27:48.516
There's plenty to go around.

00:27:48.560 --> 00:27:50.425
Oh, you're quite welcome.

00:27:53.599 --> 00:27:55.499
Is he another Sage?

00:27:55.534 --> 00:27:57.866
Have you ever seen
a Sage give away money?

00:28:00.172 --> 00:28:03.073
"Grand proxy, avoidance of..."

00:28:03.108 --> 00:28:04.837
Mm-mm.

00:28:04.876 --> 00:28:08.175
"Grand proxy, censure by..."

00:28:10.916 --> 00:28:13.384
"Grand proxy,
encounters with..."

00:28:15.053 --> 00:28:17.578
"See 'hopeless situation."'

00:28:17.623 --> 00:28:19.682
I told you there was no rule.

00:28:19.725 --> 00:28:23.456
Then it's time to invoke
the unwritten rule.

00:28:23.495 --> 00:28:25.520
The unwritten rule?

00:28:25.564 --> 00:28:28.465
When no appropriate
rule applies...

00:28:28.500 --> 00:28:29.467
make one up.

00:28:30.502 --> 00:28:32.197
That's a very good rule.

00:28:32.237 --> 00:28:33.829
Now, let's see.

00:28:33.872 --> 00:28:35.703
What should it be?

00:28:37.309 --> 00:28:41.575
The Grand Proxy is the Nagus's
official messenger, right?

00:28:43.081 --> 00:28:45.140
I've got it.

00:28:45.183 --> 00:28:48.584
When the messenger comes
to appropriate your profits...

00:28:50.422 --> 00:28:52.754
kill the messenger.

00:28:58.130 --> 00:29:00.257
Thank you!
Thank you!

00:29:19.751 --> 00:29:20.911
Arridor!

00:29:20.986 --> 00:29:22.817
Kol!

00:29:22.854 --> 00:29:24.583
Show yourselves!

00:29:24.623 --> 00:29:27.524
We can't keep
the Grand Nagus waiting!

00:29:27.559 --> 00:29:30.426
If you say so.

00:29:30.462 --> 00:29:32.020
What is the meaning of this?

00:29:32.064 --> 00:29:35.158
You're not very bright
for a Grand Proxy.

00:29:35.200 --> 00:29:38.363
Ex-Grand Proxy.

00:29:38.403 --> 00:29:40.871
But the Grand Nagus...

00:29:40.906 --> 00:29:43.170
Is on the other side
of the galaxy.

00:29:57.089 --> 00:29:58.750
Wait!

00:29:58.790 --> 00:29:59.950
I'm not...

00:30:00.025 --> 00:30:02.255
I'm not the Grand Proxy.

00:30:02.294 --> 00:30:04.819
Oh, no?
Who are you then?

00:30:04.863 --> 00:30:07.957
Stop! My name is Neelix.

00:30:08.066 --> 00:30:10.967
Neelix?
That's not a Ferengi name.

00:30:14.906 --> 00:30:15.873
Wait!

00:30:15.907 --> 00:30:18.137
I'm not Ferengi.

00:30:18.176 --> 00:30:19.234
What?

00:30:20.278 --> 00:30:23.247
I've never even met
the Grand Nagus.

00:30:23.281 --> 00:30:25.078
A likely story.

00:30:25.117 --> 00:30:26.084
It's true.

00:30:26.118 --> 00:30:27.915
I'm wearing a disguise.

00:30:27.953 --> 00:30:30.751
I'm really a Talaxian,
a crewman on Voyager.

00:30:31.823 --> 00:30:33.381
If you're not Ferengi,

00:30:33.425 --> 00:30:34.392
prove it!

00:30:34.426 --> 00:30:36.587
I'm not sure how.

00:30:41.767 --> 00:30:43.564
Doesn't that hurt?

00:30:43.602 --> 00:30:45.069
I can't feel a thing.

00:30:48.540 --> 00:30:51.270
He really isn't a Ferengi.

00:30:53.478 --> 00:30:54.843
On your feet.

00:30:56.848 --> 00:31:01.911
All right, Talaxian,
back to your ship.

00:31:01.953 --> 00:31:03.818
And tell those hu-mans

00:31:03.855 --> 00:31:05.880
to keep their hands
out of our pockets...

00:31:05.924 --> 00:31:07.653
or else.

00:31:08.760 --> 00:31:10.625
And stay out!

00:31:22.107 --> 00:31:24.337
We won. We won!

00:31:24.376 --> 00:31:26.071
No, my friend.

00:31:26.111 --> 00:31:27.806
Not exactly.

00:31:27.846 --> 00:31:29.541
To be precise...

00:31:29.581 --> 00:31:31.412
we won again.

00:31:52.237 --> 00:31:53.534
What happened?

00:31:53.572 --> 00:31:57.303
Suffice it to say, they know
I'm not the Grand Proxy.

00:31:57.342 --> 00:31:58.502
Oh, great.

00:31:58.543 --> 00:32:00.875
Let's get to the shuttle.

00:32:02.447 --> 00:32:03.937
Who are you?

00:32:04.015 --> 00:32:05.846
I'm... uh...

00:32:05.884 --> 00:32:06.851
well...

00:32:06.885 --> 00:32:09.149
You are another Holy One,
aren't you?

00:32:10.222 --> 00:32:11.712
That's right.

00:32:11.756 --> 00:32:13.883
Uh... another Holy One.

00:32:13.925 --> 00:32:15.483
Then you'll appreciate this.

00:32:15.527 --> 00:32:18.155
"The Sages in the sky did dwell

00:32:18.196 --> 00:32:20.858
"upon white clouds
that held them well,

00:32:20.899 --> 00:32:22.958
"until the sentry rang the bell,

00:32:23.068 --> 00:32:26.663
the Holy Sages never fell."

00:32:26.705 --> 00:32:28.900
That'll be three frangs, please.

00:32:28.940 --> 00:32:31.875
But we didn't ask you
to recite it.

00:32:31.910 --> 00:32:33.571
You heard it, didn't you?

00:32:33.612 --> 00:32:36.080
Your poem's very nice,
but we're in a hurry.

00:32:36.114 --> 00:32:37.445
No, please, sir.

00:32:37.482 --> 00:32:38.949
My eye.

00:32:38.984 --> 00:32:42.476
Look, friend, I'm sorry
about your eye, really, but...

00:32:42.520 --> 00:32:44.181
Wait a minute.

00:32:44.222 --> 00:32:48.249
Wasn't your patch...
on the other side?

00:32:48.293 --> 00:32:49.282
Oh.

00:32:51.997 --> 00:32:53.760
Sir?

00:32:53.798 --> 00:32:55.129
We've got to go.

00:32:55.166 --> 00:32:56.292
Wait, please.

00:32:56.334 --> 00:32:58.461
I'll throw in
another verse gratis.

00:32:58.503 --> 00:33:01.404
"But when the ringing
called them here,

00:33:01.439 --> 00:33:04.169
from the sky they did appear..."

00:33:04.209 --> 00:33:05.904
Tell me something.

00:33:05.944 --> 00:33:08.708
What happens to the Sages
at the end of the song?

00:33:08.747 --> 00:33:10.647
Oh... let me see now.

00:33:10.682 --> 00:33:12.843
The final verse.

00:33:12.884 --> 00:33:17.378
It's been a very long time,
you know.

00:33:17.422 --> 00:33:20.050
Um...

00:33:20.091 --> 00:33:22.685
Those are very handsome shoes
you have, sir.

00:33:25.363 --> 00:33:27.490
Ah, yes.

00:33:27.532 --> 00:33:29.557
It's coming back to me now.

00:33:29.601 --> 00:33:33.469
"And there amid
the eastern lights,

00:33:33.505 --> 00:33:37.236
"three new stars
appeared that night

00:33:37.275 --> 00:33:40.301
"and with the ringing
of the bell,

00:33:40.345 --> 00:33:43.212
"the Sages knew
where they must dwell.

00:33:43.248 --> 00:33:47.150
"The Holy Pilgrim led them back,

00:33:47.185 --> 00:33:50.643
"high into the sky of black

00:33:50.689 --> 00:33:54.921
"and riding
on the wings of fire,

00:33:54.960 --> 00:33:58.452
the holy men
rose higher and higher..."

00:34:00.632 --> 00:34:02.623
Wait a minute.

00:34:02.667 --> 00:34:04.897
I know who you are.

00:34:32.530 --> 00:34:35.328
I am the Holy Pilgrim.

00:34:49.748 --> 00:34:50.840
Did you hear that?

00:34:50.882 --> 00:34:51.906
The Holy Pilgrim.

00:34:51.950 --> 00:34:52.917
The Holy Pilgrim?

00:34:52.951 --> 00:34:53.975
The Holy Pilgrim!

00:34:54.085 --> 00:34:57.179
The Holy Pilgrim!
The Holy Pilgrim!

00:35:09.634 --> 00:35:12.330
I have come
to fulfill the destiny

00:35:12.370 --> 00:35:15.066
that is prophesied
in "The Song of the Sages."

00:35:15.106 --> 00:35:19.600
What in the name of eternal
destitution is going on here?

00:35:19.644 --> 00:35:21.043
Ah, there you are.

00:35:21.079 --> 00:35:23.343
Do you not recognize me?

00:35:23.381 --> 00:35:25.941
I am the Holy Pilgrim.

00:35:26.017 --> 00:35:27.348
The Holy Pilgrim?

00:35:27.385 --> 00:35:29.285
Who's the Holy Pilgrim?

00:35:29.320 --> 00:35:30.617
Quiet, you idiot.

00:35:30.655 --> 00:35:33.852
This man is no Holy Pilgrim.

00:35:33.892 --> 00:35:35.757
He's a Talaxian!

00:35:35.794 --> 00:35:36.988
Talaxian?

00:35:38.229 --> 00:35:41.062
Oh, no, Great Sage.
You are mistaken.

00:35:41.099 --> 00:35:43.260
I am indeed the Holy Pilgrim

00:35:43.301 --> 00:35:46.532
and just as "The Song
of the Sages" promises,

00:35:46.571 --> 00:35:51.599
I have come to lead you back,
high into the sky of black."

00:35:53.878 --> 00:35:56.073
I have prayed
for this day to come.

00:35:56.114 --> 00:35:58.844
Lead them back.

00:35:58.883 --> 00:36:03.149
Lead them back.
Lead them back. Lead them back.

00:36:03.188 --> 00:36:06.290
Lead them back.
Lead them back.

00:36:06.423 --> 00:36:07.754
What do they mean, lead us back?

00:36:07.791 --> 00:36:08.758
I don't know.

00:36:08.792 --> 00:36:10.760
It must be part of the song.

00:36:10.794 --> 00:36:12.921
I told you we should've
listened to the whole thing.

00:36:12.996 --> 00:36:14.463
Well, it looks as though you two

00:36:14.498 --> 00:36:16.932
will be heading off to see
the Grand Nagus after all.

00:36:17.000 --> 00:36:19.298
We'll see about that.

00:36:19.336 --> 00:36:21.099
This man...

00:36:21.138 --> 00:36:23.868
This man?

00:36:23.907 --> 00:36:26.034
Is a false pilgrim.

00:36:28.812 --> 00:36:30.712
He's come to steal your profits.

00:36:31.748 --> 00:36:34.410
I'm not a false pilgrim

00:36:34.451 --> 00:36:35.941
and I'll prove it.

00:36:36.053 --> 00:36:37.315
That's our cue.

00:36:37.354 --> 00:36:38.821
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:36:38.855 --> 00:36:39.879
On my mark.

00:36:39.923 --> 00:36:42.357
Stand by to initiate
the photon burst, Mr. Kim.

00:36:42.392 --> 00:36:43.518
Aye, Captain.

00:36:43.560 --> 00:36:45.585
Captain, I am still unable
to penetrate

00:36:45.629 --> 00:36:47.460
the Ferengi dampening field.

00:36:47.497 --> 00:36:49.362
If the away team
experiences difficulties,

00:36:49.399 --> 00:36:51.230
we will be unable
to beam them out.

00:36:51.268 --> 00:36:52.360
Keep working on it.

00:36:52.402 --> 00:36:53.369
In the meantime,

00:36:53.403 --> 00:36:54.893
we'll just have to rely
on their ingenuity

00:36:54.938 --> 00:36:57.099
to get themselves out of there
if trouble arises.

00:36:59.042 --> 00:37:01.840
The song says that

00:37:01.878 --> 00:37:05.905
"Amid the eastern lights,
three new stars

00:37:05.982 --> 00:37:07.415
appeared that night."

00:37:08.819 --> 00:37:10.878
Look, my friends.

00:37:10.921 --> 00:37:11.888
Look.

00:37:11.922 --> 00:37:12.889
Right up there.

00:37:12.923 --> 00:37:13.753
Now.

00:37:13.790 --> 00:37:15.348
Initiating photon bursts.

00:37:23.800 --> 00:37:25.700
It's a trick.

00:37:25.736 --> 00:37:27.294
He's a fraud, I tell you.

00:37:27.337 --> 00:37:29.737
Kafar, arrest this man.

00:37:31.141 --> 00:37:32.870
Well, arrest him!

00:37:39.649 --> 00:37:40.775
Ow! Stop!

00:37:40.817 --> 00:37:41.841
My ears!

00:37:41.885 --> 00:37:43.910
What do you think you're doing?!

00:37:43.954 --> 00:37:47.481
Like the song says,
Lesser Sage...

00:37:47.524 --> 00:37:49.219
"With the ringing of the bell,

00:37:49.259 --> 00:37:52.558
the Sages knew
where they must dwell."

00:37:54.731 --> 00:37:57.029
Ow!

00:37:59.169 --> 00:38:04.402
Like the song says,
you Sages, it's time for you

00:38:04.441 --> 00:38:06.068
to go back where you came from.

00:38:06.109 --> 00:38:07.508
Yes! Yes!

00:38:07.544 --> 00:38:09.011
To the sky!

00:38:09.045 --> 00:38:12.776
And they must go
on wings of fire!

00:38:12.816 --> 00:38:15.182
Wings of fire! Wings of fire!

00:38:15.218 --> 00:38:18.244
Wings of fire!
Wings of fire!

00:38:18.288 --> 00:38:19.812
Wings of fire!

00:38:25.896 --> 00:38:27.625
We are your gods!
This is outrageous!

00:38:29.833 --> 00:38:31.698
- Look, we are your gods.
- I am your god.

00:38:31.735 --> 00:38:33.100
We're the Sages.

00:38:33.136 --> 00:38:34.967
Hands off of your god.

00:38:38.408 --> 00:38:39.807
No. No.

00:38:39.843 --> 00:38:41.140
Wait a minute, people.

00:38:41.178 --> 00:38:44.045
There's no reason to interpret

00:38:44.080 --> 00:38:46.947
"The Song of the Sages"
so literally.

00:38:47.050 --> 00:38:48.176
Kafar!

00:38:48.218 --> 00:38:49.776
Kafar! Stop them!

00:38:49.820 --> 00:38:52.721
We are fulfilling
the destiny of the Sages.

00:38:52.756 --> 00:38:55.486
I am the Holy Pilgrim
and I have come to tell you

00:38:55.525 --> 00:38:58.619
that there's another verse
to the song.

00:38:58.662 --> 00:39:00.095
It's uh, uh...

00:39:00.130 --> 00:39:02.189
Please, don't burn
the Holy Ones.

00:39:02.232 --> 00:39:05.429
I am sorry, Holy Pilgrim,
but that's not part of the song.

00:39:08.038 --> 00:39:10.199
Wings of fire! Wings of fire!

00:39:10.240 --> 00:39:12.071
Wings of fire!

00:39:12.108 --> 00:39:15.236
Commander, I think now
would be a very good time

00:39:15.278 --> 00:39:16.609
for that beam-out.

00:39:20.584 --> 00:39:23.382
Wings of fire! Wings of fire!

00:39:23.420 --> 00:39:26.412
Wings of fire!
Wings of fire!

00:39:26.456 --> 00:39:28.424
Wings of fire! Wings of fire!

00:39:28.458 --> 00:39:29.925
We've got to disable
the dampening field,

00:39:29.993 --> 00:39:31.153
so they can beam us
out of here.

00:39:31.194 --> 00:39:32.161
Where's the generator?

00:39:32.195 --> 00:39:33.787
In the vault!

00:39:33.830 --> 00:39:36.094
Wings of fire!
Wings of fire!

00:39:36.132 --> 00:39:40.796
Wings of fire!
Wings of fire! Wings of fire!

00:39:40.837 --> 00:39:44.933
Wings of fire! Wings of fire!
Wings of fire!

00:39:44.975 --> 00:39:47.842
We still cannot establish
a transporter lock, Captain.

00:39:47.878 --> 00:39:50.312
Boosting power to the
annular confinement beam.

00:40:03.527 --> 00:40:04.960
Arridor?

00:40:05.028 --> 00:40:06.359
What is it now?

00:40:06.396 --> 00:40:09.957
We had seven years
of pure profit.

00:40:10.000 --> 00:40:12.935
We did, didn't we?

00:40:14.905 --> 00:40:16.600
I can't shut it down.

00:40:18.942 --> 00:40:20.705
Stand back.

00:40:33.857 --> 00:40:36.553
The Holy Ones have ascended!

00:40:39.296 --> 00:40:41.127
Is everyone okay down there,
Commander?

00:40:41.164 --> 00:40:42.461
We're all here
in one piece, Captain.

00:40:42.499 --> 00:40:43.466
Good work.

00:40:43.500 --> 00:40:44.558
Report to the Bridge

00:40:44.601 --> 00:40:46.000
as soon as everything
is in order.

00:40:46.102 --> 00:40:48.866
We'll be entering the wormhole
in approximately seven minutes.

00:40:48.905 --> 00:40:50.099
Acknowledged.

00:40:51.608 --> 00:40:53.974
We're not going
through any wormhole

00:40:54.010 --> 00:40:55.807
without our possessions.

00:40:55.845 --> 00:40:57.745
Listen, friend, you're
lucky to be alive.

00:40:57.781 --> 00:40:59.806
We beamed your shuttle
to the Shuttle Bay.

00:40:59.849 --> 00:41:01.578
As for the rest
of your possessions,

00:41:01.618 --> 00:41:02.949
they're back in the hands
of the people

00:41:03.019 --> 00:41:04.213
you stole them from.

00:41:04.254 --> 00:41:07.553
Ensign Murphy, escort these...
men to secured quarters.

00:41:07.591 --> 00:41:09.559
This is outrageous.

00:41:09.593 --> 00:41:11.754
I'll hold you
personally responsible

00:41:11.795 --> 00:41:13.695
for any losses we suffer.

00:41:13.730 --> 00:41:15.197
We'll sue!

00:41:19.736 --> 00:41:21.533
Shield status, Mr. Tuvok.

00:41:21.571 --> 00:41:22.538
Shields are optimal.

00:41:22.572 --> 00:41:24.403
Mr. Paris,
engage maneuvering thrusters

00:41:24.441 --> 00:41:25.601
and ease us into position.

00:41:25.642 --> 00:41:26.609
Aye, Captain.

00:41:26.643 --> 00:41:27.974
Sick Bay to Lieutenant Tuvok.

00:41:28.078 --> 00:41:29.170
Go ahead, Doctor.

00:41:29.212 --> 00:41:32.238
Ensign Murphy was just found
unconscious on Deck 2.

00:41:32.282 --> 00:41:33.806
It's a severe concussion.

00:41:33.850 --> 00:41:34.874
We suspect foul play.

00:41:34.918 --> 00:41:37.978
Murphy was escorting the Ferengi
to their quarters.

00:41:38.088 --> 00:41:41.114
Captain, security has been
breached in the Shuttle Bay.

00:41:41.157 --> 00:41:42.715
Seal that airlock, Mr. Tuvok.

00:41:45.195 --> 00:41:47.322
The Ferengi have phasered
the Shuttle Bay door.

00:41:47.364 --> 00:41:48.763
They are exiting the ship.

00:41:48.798 --> 00:41:51.289
Activating emergency
containment field.

00:41:55.839 --> 00:41:57.704
They're setting a course
for the planet, Captain.

00:41:57.741 --> 00:41:59.470
Lock a tractor beam
on to that shuttle.

00:41:59.509 --> 00:42:01.340
The gravitational effects
of the wormhole

00:42:01.378 --> 00:42:02.675
are refracting the beam.

00:42:02.712 --> 00:42:03.770
I can't get a lock.

00:42:03.813 --> 00:42:05.440
The Ferengi are hailing us,
Captain.

00:42:05.482 --> 00:42:06.574
On screen.

00:42:07.851 --> 00:42:11.912
Thank you for all
your assistance, hu-mans.

00:42:11.955 --> 00:42:15.686
It was lovely
doing business with you.

00:42:15.725 --> 00:42:17.955
We'll be heading back into orbit

00:42:18.061 --> 00:42:21.155
to transport
our acquisitions aboard.

00:42:24.200 --> 00:42:26.998
Beam those men back now,
Mr. Kim.

00:42:28.271 --> 00:42:31.138
I'm trying, but the targeting
scanners are out of phase.

00:42:31.174 --> 00:42:32.266
Try setting the scanners

00:42:32.308 --> 00:42:34.640
to a narrow-band
subspace frequency.

00:42:36.913 --> 00:42:38.141
What is it?

00:42:38.181 --> 00:42:40.706
They're trying to beam us
back to their ship again.

00:42:40.750 --> 00:42:44.186
They're using some sort
of subspace carrier wave.

00:42:44.220 --> 00:42:45.187
Do something!

00:42:45.221 --> 00:42:46.688
Shields to maximum.

00:42:46.723 --> 00:42:48.782
Shields are at maximum!

00:42:48.825 --> 00:42:52.090
Send out a high-energy
graviton pulse.

00:42:52.128 --> 00:42:55.586
Let's see their transporter
signal cut through that.

00:42:55.632 --> 00:42:58.999
Captain, the Ferengi are
emitting a graviton pulse.

00:42:59.035 --> 00:43:01.333
It's throwing the targeting
scanners off again.

00:43:01.371 --> 00:43:04.898
Not only that, it's
destabilizing the wormhole.

00:43:06.976 --> 00:43:08.944
Captain, a gravitational eddy
from the wormhole

00:43:08.978 --> 00:43:10.445
is attracting
the Ferengi shuttle.

00:43:10.480 --> 00:43:12.209
They're being pulled in.

00:43:15.752 --> 00:43:17.276
Reverse thrusters!

00:43:17.320 --> 00:43:19.015
They're off-line!

00:43:26.096 --> 00:43:28.860
Follow them in before that
wormhole collapses, Mr. Paris.

00:43:28.898 --> 00:43:29.956
Aye, Captain.

00:43:29.999 --> 00:43:31.261
Resetting the coordinates.

00:43:33.970 --> 00:43:36.962
Captain, the entrance
to the wormhole is moving.

00:43:37.073 --> 00:43:38.506
The Ferengi graviton pulse

00:43:38.541 --> 00:43:40.736
must have increased
its rotational momentum.

00:43:40.777 --> 00:43:43.007
Adjusting course to follow.

00:43:45.181 --> 00:43:46.341
It's too fast for us, Captain.

00:43:46.382 --> 00:43:47.440
I need more speed.

00:43:47.484 --> 00:43:50.419
Mr. Tuvok, divert auxiliary
power to the thrusters.

00:43:51.588 --> 00:43:52.816
It's not enough.

00:43:52.856 --> 00:43:55.654
Initiate a high intensity
impulse burst.

00:44:00.196 --> 00:44:03.131
Mr. Kim, reinitiate
the verteron field.

00:44:03.166 --> 00:44:05.066
Maybe we can attract
the wormhole back.

00:44:05.101 --> 00:44:07.092
The Ferengi graviton pulse
knocked the wormhole

00:44:07.137 --> 00:44:09.230
completely off
its subspace axis.

00:44:09.272 --> 00:44:12.070
It's jumping erratically
now on both ends.

00:44:12.108 --> 00:44:14.576
Options?

00:44:20.583 --> 00:44:22.175
There are none.

00:44:27.657 --> 00:44:32.617
Mr. Paris, reset a course
for the Alpha Quadrant.

00:44:32.662 --> 00:44:34.960
Warp 6.

00:44:35.064 --> 00:44:36.759
Aye, Captain.

00:44:51.114 --> 00:44:52.672
Look.

00:44:52.715 --> 00:44:55.013
The Holy Ones are going home!
